{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:39:53.867770Z","id":"e04b8c11caf126353cf9d2f79d36927d8b8a56c066277f04807dd8f64de7eb35","body":{"detail":"Background.swift has no unit test target: margin, ackWait, tick and remaining are stored properties a test could set, but no ios_unit_test exists. The simulator showed only the trim on leaving (os_log 'Clax trim began' / 'Clax trim ended', and 'trimmed memory' in daemon.log) and the trim on a memory warning (written to <device>/data/var/run/memory_warning_simulation). No caller sends pauseDone yet (lib/platform/background_work.dart IosBackgroundWork.pauseDone has no caller in lib/), so every pause waits the full ackWait before trimming.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"ab367a42378343bb7f18d635c145567a5ad05658a8820f689412366279a55653"},"suggested_fix":"Drive the DEBUG expireBackgroundTask hook from a simulator integration test with a run recorded, and check the 'Clax run pausing' / 'Clax run paused' / 'Clax run ended' lines and the stopped call in Dart.","summary":"The pause path (the 5 s margin, the expiration handler, the 2 s wait for pauseDone, then trim and end) has no automated test","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:02.421779Z","id":"32f8b7a302b21c9c51f8acc381846117ae0594eb687cf6a634ceaea595bdd921","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e04b8c11caf126353cf9d2f79d36927d8b8a56c066277f04807dd8f64de7eb35","summary":"pauseDone now has a caller: AppRoot._pauseRuns (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) sends it after AppPresence.pause and the paused notice (test/app_background_test.dart 'on iOS the change is paused with one notice, then pauseDone; ...'). The Swift pause path itself is still untested, so this stays open.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:17:32.807501Z","id":"94d49a112c5d373248c6f6098e732f6bc91f5e2873fbde918cc26acf28e72dc6","body":{"detail":"The manifest declares one collected data type, NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherUserContent (linked false, tracking false, purpose AppFunctionality), as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md §10.4 drafts it: what the person types or says, and their app's code, go to Anthropic's Claude API under the person's own API key; Clax's developer receives nothing. The spec's open question 7 (same file, 'The privacy label (blocks external TestFlight)') asks the owner to confirm this reading. Options: (a) keep it; (b) declare nothing collected, on the reading that data sent to a third party under the person's own key at their request is not collected by the developer; (c) another type or purpose. The App Store Connect privacy label must agree with whatever is chosen. apps/clax_app/tool/ios-app-check.sh asserts the current entry field by field, so a change edits both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"b6136698b4103ce8c2abcc14fed4ab3e51a0aabe801bd536b30ef32f251edf35"},"summary":"Owner decision: are the person's requests and app code, sent to Anthropic under the person's own key, 'Other User Content' for App Functionality, not linked, not tracking?","tags":["status:needs-decision","ios","privacy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:17:32.807581Z","id":"a6b7dd3d8e97f5b1a50791400396c43e20165e7f0a9886aeba33021952ee1212","body":{"detail":"nm -u on the simulator Clax.app/Clax imports _statfs and _fstatfs; in libclax_ios.a only the libsqlite3-sys object imports them. libsqlite3-sys 0.30.1's sqlite3.c (unixOpen, around line 44826) calls fstatfs to compare f_fstypename with msdos/exfat, and statfs in its locking-style and proxy paths. None of Apple's DiskSpace reasons (85F4.1, E174.1, 7D9E.1, B728.1) describes a file-system type check; E174.1 is the nearest, since the check precedes writes to the database. App Store review accepts or rejects the reason; ios-app-check.sh fails if a DiskSpace symbol disappears from or appears in the binary without the manifest following.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"0e5d12db64042e414672c08ad84cd1cd937408ebc7c0543a266c9b0a30b88b0c"},"summary":"DiskSpace is declared with E174.1 (free space before a write), but the binary's only statfs/fstatfs caller, SQLite, reads the file system's type, not its free space","tags":["ios","privacy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
